    <h2>The honest answer</h2>
    <p><strong>If you are a publisher (news site, magazine, multi-author blog, content membership), WordPress is the right tool.</strong> The editorial workflow is what it was built for.</p>
    <p><strong>If you are a service business with 5&ndash;10 pages and a contact form, WordPress is overkill and structurally insecure.</strong> You are paying for an editorial CMS you do not need, while inheriting a security maintenance burden you cannot manage. A custom-coded static site is genuinely the right shape.</p>
